<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="AVI 120" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2009" href="schedule/2009.xml">2009</calendarYear><term id="120091" href="schedule/2009/spring.xml">Spring 2009</term><subject id="AVI" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI.xml">Aviation</subject></parents><label>Private Pilot II</label><description>Second of a two course sequence to prepare for FAA Private Pilot certification. Includes classroom instruction on airplane operation, navigation, night flying and meteorology. Includes 34.5 hours of flight training and 3 hours in a flight simulator in the flight laboratory. Students enrolling in this course will also participate in up to 5 hours of research flight experiments. Students successfully completing final examinations will be issued a Private Pilot certificate. Credit is not given for both AVI 120 and AVI 121. Prerequisite: AVI 101 and consent of director. </description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sections><section id="30095" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30095.xml">AE1</section><section id="30096" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30096.xml">AE2</section><section id="30097" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30097.xml">AFA</section><section id="30098" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30098.xml">AFB</section><section id="30099" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30099.xml">AFC</section><section id="30100" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30100.xml">AFD</section><section id="30101" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30101.xml">AFE</section><section id="30127" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30127.xml">AFF</section><section id="30132" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30132.xml">AFG</section><section id="30136" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30136.xml">AFH</section><section id="30145" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30145.xml">AFI</section><section id="30150" href="schedule/2009/spring/AVI/120/30150.xml">A